WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:12,290
How many times per day can I run my day programs?

00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:17,490
Well, you could run your day programs over and over and over and over throughout the day.

00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:23,570
So there isn't a limit to running your day programs. The only thing that I would say is if

00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:29,330
you are going to be fairly non-ambulatory and you're going to be sitting and reading for

00:00:30,370 --> 00:00:35,570
considerable length of time, let's say eight hours, just run your night program again,

00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:40,930
so you don't have to hit, you know, open up your computer and hit run because your day programs are

00:00:40,930 --> 00:00:47,010
only an hour to two hours long. So then just run your night program if you're going to be sitting

00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:55,490
there for a long time. So, um, but let's say you got two hours here and other two hours later on

00:00:55,490 --> 00:01:01,010
and another two hours tonight before you go to bed, then go ahead and run your day programs three times.

00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:07,650
I've always said you could explore other programs if you have other cold morbidities, you know,

00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:13,090
you might have an infection or you might have, you know, you feel like cold is coming on or something

00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:20,130
like that. Go ahead and run those programs at your will. Especially if your cancer is, you know,

00:01:20,130 --> 00:01:28,850
do eat well, but if your cancer is, you know, not in the do eat well phase and it is a very active

00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:33,650
that I would spend the majority of my time running cancer programs. When I was in the throes of my

00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:40,850
cancer, I was only running my cancer programs and I was running at, you know, at night, actually,

00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:47,410
as soon as I got home, I was so, you know, I just, I was still going to work, but I was basically

00:01:47,490 --> 00:01:53,410
working from my desk like I'm sitting right now the entire day. So I was running my right at the

00:01:53,410 --> 00:02:00,450
office. I had a rife running and I ran that the whole day and I went home and when I was really ill,

00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:05,090
I wasn't doing anything. I was going home and sitting in my chair and turned down the rife and I was

00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:10,610
running the rife and then when I went to bed, I turned it out. So I was literally running it almost

00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:20,050
24-7 when I was in the throes of it. I mean, obviously, I wasn't 24-7 because I was, you know, living,

00:02:20,050 --> 00:02:25,890
you know, up and doing stuff. But every time I was sitting doing nothing, which when I was really sick,

00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:32,850
it was a lot of time when I was sitting doing a whole little lot of nothing, I was running the

00:02:32,850 --> 00:02:38,370
rife. So, you know, when you're in the throes of the cancer, the more rife time you could get the

00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:46,450
better chance you have that survival. So, I really believe that it was the action of the rife

00:02:46,450 --> 00:02:54,290
machine that put me in the state of remission that I'm in right now. So, don't not run your rife

00:02:54,290 --> 00:02:59,970
when you are sitting. Now, I do want you to be living it up and doing things and living your life. But

00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:05,730
if you are exhausted, you have to sit down and you're going to rest and I got to I'll go read a book or

00:03:05,730 --> 00:03:13,330
I'm going to read my Bible, then turn out the rife and be doing you're running the rife.

